        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Dixon Residential Estate Agents are delighted to present 87 Oak Way to the Meath property market.\r\n\r\nThis well-proportioned three-bedroom family home offers generous living accommodation, excellent outdoor space and ample off-street parking, making it an ideal choice for first-time buyers, families and investors alike.\r\n\r\nOn entering the property, you are greeted by a spacious entrance hallway which leads into the living room. Through the interconnecting doors, you are brought into the bright kitchen/dining room, which is located to the rear of the property and provides an excellent space for everyday family living. A convenient bathroom is also located beneath the stairs.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises two generous double bedrooms, a single bedroom and a family bathroom. The property further benefits from a well-maintained rear garden, while the spacious front garden provides ample off-street parking.\r\n\r\nOak Way is ideally located close to a wide range of local amenities in Johnstown. A selection of primary and secondary schools are within easy reach, including St Stephen’s National School, Coláiste na Mí and Loreto Secondary School. Johnstown Shopping Centre, SuperValu and the IDA Business Park are also conveniently located nearby.\r\n\r\nThe area benefits from excellent transport links, with easy access to the M3 motorway providing convenient connectivity to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. Dublin City Centre is approximately a 50-minute drive, subject to traffic conditions.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to appreciate the generous accommodation, outdoor space and excellent location this family home has to offer.\r\n\r\nAll information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost care and attention have been placed in providing factual and correct information. In certain cases, some information may have been provided to us by the vendor. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors, or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have."
